# End-to-end flow from the original README, sent through the gateway.
# Works with the VS Code REST Client extension, Rider and Visual Studio.

@gateway = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Add driver locations
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/locations/drivers/update
Content-Type: application/json

{ "driverId": "driver:1", "latitude": 12.9716, "longitude": 77.5946 }

###
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/locations/drivers/update
Content-Type: application/json

{ "driverId": "driver:2", "latitude": 12.9800, "longitude": 77.5800 }

###
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/locations/drivers/update
Content-Type: application/json

{ "driverId": "driver:3", "latitude": 12.9600, "longitude": 77.6100 }

### Nearby drivers
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/locations/drivers/nearby?latitude=12.9716&longitude=77.5946&radius=5

### All drivers (with busy flag)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/locations/drivers/

### Fare estimate (new)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/rides/estimate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "pickupLatitude": 12.9716, "pickupLongitude": 77.5946, "dropLatitude": 12.9352, "dropLongitude": 77.6245 }

### 2. Request a ride
# @name requestRide
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/rides/request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "riderId": "rider:1",
  "pickupLatitude": 12.9716,
  "pickupLongitude": 77.5946,
  "pickupAddress": "MG Road, Bangalore",
  "dropLatitude": 12.9352,
  "dropLongitude": 77.6245,
  "dropAddress": "Koramangala, Bangalore"
}

### 3. Check ride status (expect driverId + status ACCEPTED after a moment)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/rides/{{requestRide.response.body.id}}

### Driver is arriving (new)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/rides/{{requestRide.response.body.id}}/arriving

### 4. Start the ride
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/rides/{{requestRide.response.body.id}}/start

### 5. Complete the ride
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/rides/{{requestRide.response.body.id}}/complete

### Cancel (only valid before completion)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/rides/{{requestRide.response.body.id}}/cancel?reason=Changed%20plans

### 6. Rider history
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/rides/rider/rider:1

### Driver history (new)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/rides/driver/driver:1

### Validation error example → 400 problem details
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/rides/request
Content-Type: application/json

{ "riderId": "", "pickupLatitude": 123 }

### Driver goes offline
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/v1/locations/drivers/driver:3
